Normally one would expect that smashing a potion (of any sort) on a 
footrice will stone you. That much is reasonable. It's also arguable 
that after changing a foe to a footrice in this manner you should also 
be stoned, as happened. Depending on whether the potion effect comes 
before or after the check for stoning, one of these would be possible.

 From the OP there is a stoning check after the potion effect, but there 
could also be one before, to cover both cases. I just tested this and 
there is only one check for stoning; smashing a !polymorph on a footrice 
does not stone you, you only get the effect of the new creature (a 
spotted jelly's acid, in my case).

Almost certainly a bug, but you could argue that you only touch your 
target with the follow through, after it changes. I would suggest 
checking for monster effects on both sides of the potion effect, but 
you'd have to make sure not to duplicate for non-polymorph potions.


